course: dictionary
lesson: 1773
title: Cleverness and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cleverness means being clever: learning quickly, understanding things well and thinking of good ideas. The ending -ness turns clever into a noun, a name for the quality. So a clever person has cleverness.
explain: The word has a second meaning too: being tricky or cunning. Context tells you which one is meant. «Babe's cleverness is real, though: pigs solve puzzles as well as many dogs» shows the good meaning, because solving puzzles is a sign of a quick mind.
explain: Cleverness is not the same as size. «An elephant brain weighs about 5 kilograms, the largest of any land animal, but a big body needs a big brain, so size alone does not show cleverness.» The clue words are size alone does not show, so being big and being clever are different things.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. In «through cleverness», if you swap in «by being quick and smart» and the sentence still makes sense, you have understood it.
fact: Cleverness is a noun: it names the quality of being clever.
fact: «Cleverness» means being quick to learn, understand and think of good ideas.
fact: «Cleverness» can also mean being tricky or cunning.
fact: In stories, cleverness often beats strength: a small character can use cleverness to beat a giant.
fact: At school, cleverness is praised, but effort matters too.
exercise: «Babe's cleverness is real: pigs solve puzzles as well as many dogs.» What does cleverness mean here? | Being tricky to get what you want | *Being quick to learn and solve problems | Being very big and strong | Being sleepy after lunch
exercise: «An elephant brain is the largest of any land animal, but size alone does not show cleverness.» What does this sentence tell you? | *Being big does not prove that an animal is clever | Elephants have tiny brains | Big animals are always the cleverest | Size and cleverness are the same thing
exercise: Which word is the noun for being clever? | *cleverness | cleverly | clevered | clever
test: In «a small character uses cleverness to beat a giant», what does cleverness help the character do? | Grow bigger | Fall asleep | Hide from the giant forever | *Win by thinking well
test: Which is the second meaning of cleverness? | Being very tired | *Being tricky or cunning | Being sorry for a mistake | Being very tall
exam: Which best explains why «size alone does not show cleverness»? | *A big body does not prove a clever mind | Size and cleverness always go together | Small animals are the cleverest of all | Cleverness only grows with size
